    "abstract": "DeepONet learns nonlinear operators mapping input functions to output functions, motivated by the universal approximation theorem for operators. A branch net encodes the input function sampled at fixed sensors and a trunk net encodes the output location; their inner product gives G(u)(y). Stacked and unstacked variants are evaluated on ODE/PDE operators and compared with fully connected and sequence baselines.",
    "domain": "Other",
    "key_claims": [
      "Operators can be approximated by G(u)(y) ≈ sum_k b_k(u(x_1..x_m)) t_k(y) + b_0 with branch and trunk networks.",
      "DeepONet achieves smaller generalization error than FNN baselines on the studied operators.",
      "Unstacked DeepONet with bias generalizes better than stacked DeepONet in the paper's experiments.",
      "Test error shows fast (exponential then polynomial) convergence with respect to the number of training examples."
    ],
    "parsed_at": "2026-10-23T12:00:00+05:30",
